{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1235528-shaping-rituals-for-the-gambling-sorceror","id":1235528,"title":"Shaping rituals for the gambling sorceror","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-16T06:27:04-07:00","id":1235528,"title":"Shaping rituals for the gambling sorceror","content":"Hullo!<br /> I've just started playing a character who won sorcerous initiation from Sigereth, the Player of Games in a bet. I've come up with some merits that I'm happy with, but I'm not comfortable with the shaping ritual that I've put together. It just feels like it'll be a bit unwieldy in play. I've considered the less obvious aspects of Sigereth for inspiration, but nothing's really coming into a shaping ritual for me. Something to do with her &quot;Intrigue and intricate stratagems trump brute force&quot; could maybe be cool. Or something that punishes cheating - a shaping ritual based on her &quot;The Game is Real&quot; charm would be pretty neat. But I'm stumped as to how to actually implement it.<br /> <br /> Oh, or maybe something modeled on one of Mara's shaping rituals in the corebook, only instead of sleeping with mortals to extract their souls &amp; fuel spells, I could win... something, from people in bets and turn it into sorcerous power.<br /> <br /> I'd be grateful for any ideas, anyway.<br /> <br /> This is working idea that I'm not happy with:<br /> Shaping Ritual: The character may place bets for sorcerous motes. A fallback option is to bet initiative or temporary essence for a similar number of sorcerous motes, using the Shape Sorcery roll as the variable. A more interesting option for a variable is to \u201ccall\u201d things that will happen in the near future, with odds offered by the Storyteller. There are endless options for more interesting wagers, and the Storyteller can assign a value in motes to things the character might bet instead. (i.e. the goodwill of an NPC, an item the character possesses, or a useful thing the character knows.) Things belonging to other characters might also be used as fodder for wagers, with said character's permission","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T06:43:25-07:00","id":1235531,"title":"","content":"\u2026 Oh, it took me a moment to realise that you said Sigereth, and not Plentimon.<br /> <br /> The principle of getting sorcerous motes for winning a bet seems sound to me, but I do think the idea of putting up other mechanical resources as an ante may be out of keeping with the usual ritual.<br /> <br /> I also think that the idea of it functioning on prediction of a certain outcome is one of the better ways to do it, rather than games of chance that the system has a limited means to depict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T07:49:19-07:00","id":1235556,"title":"","content":"With predicting a certain outcome, I'm mainly worried about burdening the ST with deciding whether it's too likely, whether to give better odds on something, having to pass notes when I guess other PCs' actions... I thought it sounded fun in theory but I worry it'll be really annoying in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T14:44:45-07:00","id":1240217,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a specific easily-replicated action where chance is the dominant factor. The flipping of a coin, the selection of a suit in a deck of cards. Picking a few with known numerical odds are as easy to replicate as rolling various sided dice. Also has decent roleplaying potential. I'm not sure if its really the mechanics you don't care for, or the imagery. If its simply the mechanics, representing chance-outcomes is just different dice. Just need to figure out what represents what odds, as needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T19:27:29-07:00","id":1240287,"title":"","content":"You could model the betting on Fate-Shifting Solar ar\u00eate? Whenever you shape sorcery declare a die-result other than ones to function as double 10s. If that number comes up treat it as double success in place of 10s. Must declare the chosen integer prior to rolling.<br /> <br /> That shouldn't mess up probabilities too much though it should have some skewing effect to the positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T20:27:02-07:00","id":1240307,"title":"","content":"I have a deck of cards idea. Get a regular deck (or a Tarot) and shuffles it. Make a bet for Suit, and Size.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Suit</b></u><br /> Right Suit: 3sm<br /> Wrong Suit, Right Color: 1sm<br /> Wrong Suit and Color: -1sm<br /> <br /> <u><b>Size</b></u><br /> Choose either a <i>Major Card</i> or a <i>Minor Card</i>. If you are correct, gain the following bonus.<br /> Major Card (Jack-Queen-King-Ace-Joker) +2sm<br /> Minor Card (2-10)+1sm<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Push Your Luck</i></u></b><br /> You may choose, after drawing the card, to gamble further. By wagering the Sorcerous Motes drawn from <i>Sigereth's Blessed Deck</i> you may challenge the Demon to a classic game of &quot;double or nothing&quot;:<br /> Flip a coin- Heads you receive double the amount of Sorcerous Motes, Tails you lose the ones you pulled from this draw (but not any others you may may have accumulated)<br /> <br /> <b><u><i>Shoot the Moon</i></u></b><br /> If you have -1 sm from this draw, instead of <i>Push Your Luck</i> you can try to gamble for higher stakes. Flip a coin- Heads, you take 1 Aggravated damage; Tails, you gain 5 SM.<br /> <br /> <br /> In theory, you could gain 10sm in one shot, but probably you'll get 2 or 3. You can even lose a mote or some health if your very unlucky. This might be closer to a minor artifact, but that's ok. Sigereth strikes me as the type who isn't too picky about who she plays with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T03:33:16-07:00","id":1241742,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the deck of cards idea. The &quot;double-or-nothing&quot; element fits nicely, too. Before being Exalted, my character bet his genius for strength enough to defeat a group of Immaculate Monks, and lost. He then panicked, offered double or nothing, agreeing to become a Baidak pawn if he lost again, but retaining his genius if he won.<br /> <br /> Sigereth asked if he'd like to try again. He declined. (While mortal, in any case.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}